capture/transport lifecycle, native bitrate/control handling and actual
ScreenCaptureKit → hardware VideoToolbox → native QUIC now pass component and
short authenticated live loopback tests. No desktop pixels were persisted.
The ordinary Client remains explicitly gated. Next connect its fixed geometry,
typed launch and explicit optional audio/cursor/input negotiation before removing
that gate. Do not invent capabilities to satisfy Linux assumptions. Live decode,
presentation, performance and complete LoginWindow lifecycle remain open.
This is not a user-testable Mac Host release. See
`macos-native-video.md`, `macos-authentication.md` and HANDOFF for exact evidence.

